JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Drug-induced haemolysis and fast haemoglobin A1 in diabetes mellitus</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1979</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1037</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">519273</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serratrice</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Granel</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Swiader</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Disdier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>de Roux- Serratrice</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Raccah</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Interference of dapsone in HbA1c monitoring of a diabetic patient with polychondritis</article-title><source>Diabetes Metab</source><year>2002</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>508</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12522333</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Albright</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Ovalle</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Artifactually low hemoglobin A1c caused by use of dapsone</article-title><source>Endocr Pract</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>370</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15259122</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Polgreen</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Putz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sta